  "persona": "",
  "subject": "A Taipei taxi driver keeps a tin box of the scrap-paper addresses passengers scribbled, reads each handwriting like a face, and one night a young man hands him a slip that only says take me home.",
  "caption": "West Coast cool-jazz chamber ballad, slow and spacious. Soft piano with sparse voicings, flute playing a legato countermelody, upright bass with warm round tone, brushed snare and quiet ride cymbal. Dry intimate jazz-club room sound. Female vocal, warm low-mid alto, tender, clearly sung melody. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 72 BPM, F major. Wistful, unhurried mood. No synthesizers, no autotune, no electric guitar, no trap drums, no rap.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n計程車的前座後壁\n我囥一盒鐵箱仔\n內底攏是乘客的紙條\n寫著伊欲去的所在\n[Pre-Chorus]\n有的字大，有的字細\n我攏會記得\n[Chorus]\n字會講話，毋免開喙\n歪的是緊，圓的是慢\n我共紙條一張一張收\n載人去，嘛載字轉\n[Verse]\n有一張寫「南京東路」\n筆劃圓圓像細粒糖仔\n我想寫的人，應該愛甜\n後來伊果然提一包予我\n[Pre-Chorus]\n有一張寫甲看袂清楚\n我問，伊講：「我緊張」\n[Chorus]\n字會講話，毋免開喙\n歪的是緊，圓的是慢\n我共紙條一張一張收\n載人去，嘛載故事轉\n[Verse]\n昨暗有一个後生人\n遞紙條，寫「予我轉去」\n無地址，無電話\n我問伊，轉去佗位\n[Bridge]\n我問伊細漢的路，就開去\n紙條囥佇鐵箱仔頂面\n[Chorus]\n字會講話，毋免開喙\n今仔日換我寫一張\n我共紙條放佇後座\n等一个人來讀\n[Outro]\n載人去，嘛載字轉\n慢慢仔，慢慢仔行",
